SUMMARY:Bodhi Day
DESCRIPTION:Bodhi Day is observed by many Buddhists in remembrance of Siddhartha Gautama’s enlightenment\, which\, according to Buddhist tradition\, he attained while meditating under the Bodhi tree. Through meditation\, reflection\, and acts of kindness\, practitioners honor the Buddhist path toward wisdom and compassion. This observance invites us to learn about Buddhist traditions and reflect on how mindfulness and compassion can strengthen our communities. \n  \nLearn more at Tricycle: The Buddhist Review.
URL:https://hatefreetogether.org/event/bodhi-day/
LOCATION:CA
CATEGORIES:Season of Connection
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://hatefreetogether.org/wp-content/uploads/Buddha.png
END:VEVENT
